[ti:Week04-Wed.mp3]

[00:00.00]contend 熟义 v. (尤指在争论中)声称，认为；竞争， 争夺 示例 ① America has at least four separate immigration problems to contend with, and only one of them is there any progress. 美国至少要解决四个相互独立的移民问题，却只有一个稍有进展。（The Economist）② Developing nations have always had to contend with infectious diseases. 发展中国家常常要与传染性疾病作斗争。
[00:07.24]alter 熟义 v. (使)改变，更改；修改(衣服使更合身) 示例 ① We do this by altering our metabolic rate, shivering or sweating. 人类通过改变自身的新陈代谢率、发抖或者出汗来实现（体温恒定）。（2008. 12） ② This doesn't alter the fact that what she did was wrong. 这改变不了她所做的是错的这一事实。
[00:12.65]provoke 熟义 v. 激起，引发；挑衅，激怒 示例 ① Others believe that she expected defeat, and was in fact using the case to provoke discussion of constitutional reform. 其他人认为她预料到自己会被击败， 事实上她在利用这起事件激起人们对宪法改革的讨论。（The Economist） ② The topic was intended to provoke heated discussion. 这个话题旨在引发热烈的讨论。
[00:19.50]arouse 熟义 v. 激起，引起（感情、态度）；激发； 唤醒 示例 ① Our research arouses the concern that people may now be more likely to raise negative views of African Americans. 我们的研究引起了人们对一种现象的关注， 即人们现在更可能对非洲裔美国人产生负面看法。（2010. 6）② The whole country was aroused by the crime last year. 去年的这一罪行激起了整个国家的愤怒。
[00:26.28]pose 熟义 v.（为画像、摄影）摆好姿势；提问； 造成（威胁、问题等）‖n. 姿势；装腔作势 示例 ① College faculty members are afraid that the pretext of moving students into the workforce might pose a threat to the core curriculum. 大学教职工担心，这种以促进学生就业为借口的行为可能会对核心课程构成威胁。（2012. 6）② The leader posed briefly for photographs before going to the conference hall. 在进入会议大厅之前，那位领导人简单地摆了一个姿势以供拍照。
[00:34.80]desirable 熟义 a. 可取的，值得拥有的 示例 ① While technological progress as a whole continually narrows our sphere of freedom, each new technical advance considered by itself appears to be desirable. 作为一个整体，技术的进步不断地压缩我们自由的范围；而作为个案，每一次新的技术进步，看上去都令人神往。（The Washington Post） ② It is a common phenomenon that it is no longer desirable for adult children to live with their parents. 孩子长大成人后便不想再与父母住在一起，这很常见。
[00:44.41]sensitive 熟义 a.（对低温、光、食物等）过敏的；（对细微变化）灵敏的；敏感的 示例 ① Fake listening may be easily exposed, since many speakers are sensitive to facial cues and can tell if you're merely pretending to listen. 假装在听很容易暴露，因为许多讲话者对面部表情都很敏感，他们能够分辨出你是否只是假装在听。（2007. 12） ② The pop singer tries her best to sidestep for sensitive issues like marriage. 那位流行歌手尽可能地回避像婚姻这类敏感的问题。
[00:53.04]feasible 熟义 a. 可行的，行得通的 示例 ① Public opinion polls show that people in most rich countries already think that immigration is too high. Further big increases would be politically unfeasible. 公众民意测验表明，大部分富裕国家的人认为移民已经太多，增加更多的移民在政治上将不可行。（2010. 12）② It is necessary for us to make a feasible plan before taking action. 在行动之前，我们有必要制订一个可行的计划。
[01:01.28]naive 熟义 a. 天真的，幼稚的 示例 ① Yet most of the kids were incredibly naive. Some had never even been to downtown Chicago. 然而，大多数的孩子天真得让人难以置信。一些孩子甚至都还没去过芝加哥市区。（The Atlantic）② She is so naive as to believe such a lie. 她竟然幼稚得连这种谎言都相信。
[01:06.69]denial 熟义 n. 否认，否定；拒绝给予，剥夺（应有的权利） 示例 ① Forget the old idea that conserving energy is a form of self-denial —riding bicycles, dimming the lights, and taking fewer showers. 忘记“节约能源就是自我牺牲”这种旧观点吧，诸如：骑自行车、 将灯光调暗和减少淋浴次数。（2007. 12） ② I think he is still in denial about her death. 我认为他仍拒绝接受她死了这一事实。 语料 All the blessings we enjoy are the fruits of labor, toil, and self-denial, and study. 我们得到的一切幸福都是劳动、辛苦、自我克制和学习的成果。（美国社会学家萨姆纳）
[01:17.01]intuition 熟义 n. 直觉力；（一种）直觉 示例 ① In a commencement speech to students at Stanford University in 2005, Steve Jobs, the chief executive of Apple, advised his audience to avoid being trapped by dogma and to have the courage to follow their hearts and their intuition. 2005年，苹果首席执行官斯蒂芬• 乔布斯在斯坦福大学毕业典礼上对学生们提出建议，不要被教条束缚，要勇于跟随自己的内心和直觉。（The Economist）② I had an intuition that some serious mistakes appeared in my final exam. 我凭直觉感到自己在期末考试中出现了一些严重的失误。
[01:27.87]bacterium 熟义 n. 细菌；[pl.] bacteria 示例 ① At any given time, however, some mice escape and run free. These mice are "pests". They can disrupt experiments with the bacteria organisms they carry. 然而，在任何特定的时间，一些老鼠都会逃脱并不受控制，这些老鼠就成了“害虫”。它们身上携带的生物细菌可能会破坏实验。（2011. 12）② The doctor told me that some bacteria are good for our health. 医生告诉我，有些细菌对我们的健康是有好处的。
[01:36.39]simplicity 熟义 n. 质朴，淳朴；简单（性），容易 （性）；简单（或质朴、朴素）之处 示例 ① In a presentation at December's news: rewired digital journalism conference, Belam said, "Think reader before editor. Think software before content. Think simplicity before features. Think mobile before desktop." 在去年12月的数字新闻大会上的演讲中，贝尔曼说道：“（我们应该）先考虑读者后考虑编辑； 先考虑软件适用性后考虑报道内容；先考虑言辞简练后考虑长篇特写；先考虑移动设备后考虑电脑。”（Journalism） ② The simplicity of the book makes it suitable for children. 这本书简单易懂，适合儿童。 语料 In a complex world, to insist upon simplicity is foolish. 在复杂的世界上，坚持单纯是愚蠢的。（美国作家理查德•沃克尔默）
[01:49.96]defendant 熟义 n. 被告人，被告 示例 ① Amador said that the defendant suffered "from severe deficits in awareness of illness."阿马多尔说被告患有严重的“疾病意识缺陷”。（The Atlantic）② The defendant was accused of pocket-picking on a bus in India. 那位被告被指控在印度的一辆公交车上偷窃。
[01:55.77]penalty 熟义 n. 惩罚，刑罚；害处，不利 示例 ① Alcohol is strictly prohibited for Muslims in Iran. Repeat offenders can even face the death penalty. 在伊朗，酒类严禁销售给伊斯兰教徒。重犯者甚至可能被判死刑。（The Economist）② He was imposed a penalty of four years' imprisonment for stealing. 他因盗窃罪被判处四年监禁。
[02:02.16]tough 熟义 a. 艰苦的；强硬的；健壮的 示例 ① Most young boys are trained to believe that men should be strong, tough, cool, and detached. 大多数男孩所受的教育都让他们相信男人应该强壮、坚强、沉着、 冷漠。（2010. 12）② I will never forget the tough time my parents experienced when I was a child. 我永远不会忘记在我小时候父母经历的艰苦岁月。
[02:08.63]silicon 熟义 n. 硅，硅元素 示例 ① There aren't many jobs in science for them, so they go to Wall Street and Silicon Valley to apply their analytical skills to more practical—and rewarding— efforts. 科学领域能给他们提供的工作机会不多，所以他们去了华尔街和硅谷，在更实际、回报更高的工作岗位上施展自己的分析才能。（2010. 12）② People tend to associate the hi-tech industry with the Silicon Valley. 人们倾向于将高科技与硅谷联系起来。
[02:17.15]professional 熟义 a. 职业的；娴熟的‖n. 自由职业者；专业人员 示例 ① Although children of Mexican immigrants do better, in terms of educational and professional attainment, than their parents, UCLA sociologist Edward Telles has found that the gains don't continue. 虽然墨西哥移民的下一代在教育和专业技能上优于他们的父母，但是加州大学洛杉矶分校的社会学家爱德华•特勒斯发现，这样的优势并没有持续下去。（2008. 12）② If it's a legal matter he need to seek professional advice. 如果这属于法律问题，他就需要进行专业咨询了。
[02:27.27]hinder 熟义 v. 阻碍，妨碍，阻挡 示例 ① Case studies of children who were isolated from others reveal that they lack a firm self-concept, and their mental and psychological development is severely hindered by lack of language. 对那些与其他人隔离开的孩子的案例分析发现他们缺乏坚定的自我概念，而且他们智力上和心理上的发展由于缺少语言而受到严重阻碍。（2010. 6）② The policy will promote rather than hinder reform. 这项政策将促进而不是妨碍改革。
[02:35.99]genius 熟义 n. 天才，天赋；本领；（某领域的）天才人物 示例 ① The three-year degree isn't a new idea. Geniuses have always breezed through. 三年制学位并非新概念。天才总能轻轻松松获得。（2012. 6）② She is a genius at cooking noodles. 她有做面条的天赋。
[02:40.75]transistor 熟义 n. 晶体管；晶体管收音机 示例 ① Like the inventors of lasers and transistors, Alan Turing—without whom the modern computer wouldn't exist—and Tim Berners-Lee, inventor of the worldwide web, did not become rich. 如同激光和晶体管的发明者一样，阿兰•图灵—— 没有他现代计算机不可能存在，以及互联网的发明者蒂姆•伯纳斯•李并没有变得富有。（The Guardian）② The TV can't display pictures because of broken transistor. 晶体管坏了，电视机无法显示图像。
[02:49.93]vessel 熟义 n. 大船，轮船；（盛液体的）容器，器皿；血管 示例 ① Threaded through a person's blood vessels, the sensor can provide blood pressure readings at the valve of the heart itself. 经过一个人的血管，这种传感器就能显示这个人心脏自身瓣膜处的血压值。（2011. 12）② Unfortunately, the vessel was caught in terrible tsunami last year. 很不幸，那艘轮船去年遭遇到了可怕的海啸。 语料 As empty vessels make the loudest sound, so they that have least wit are the greatest babblers. 正如空容器发出的声音最大，智力最低者最善于唠叨不休。（古希腊哲学家柏拉图）
[03:00.64]typical 熟义 a. 典型的；一贯的；特有的 示例 ① Picture a typical MBA lecture theatre twenty years ago. 想象一下20年前典型的工商管理硕士课堂。（2011. 6） ② That outburst was a typical example of his lack of self-control. 那次发作是他缺乏自控力的典型例子。
[03:05.55]personnel 熟义 n.（组织或军队中的）全体人员；人事部门 示例 ① Despite the modesty of the benefit, the Chamber of Commerce and other business groups fought it bitterly, describing it as "government-run personnel management" and a "dangerous precedent." 尽管这项法案带来的好处不大，却遭到了商会和其他一些商业组织的猛烈抨击，被称为“政府经营的人事管理”和“一个危险的先例”。（2010. 6） ② It is said that the personnel department is currently reviewing pay scales. 据说人事部门正在审核工资级别。
[03:15.38]executive 熟义 n.（公司或机构的）主管领导；行政部门‖a. 决策的；有执行权的；高级的 示例 ① Enter the executive editor, who makes a suggestion requiring a more-than-modest rearrangement of the design and the addition of an information box. 这时执行编辑进来了，提出一个建议，要求大幅地调整版式设计，并增加一个信息框。（2011. 6） ② He is waiting for the plane at an executive lounge. 他正在贵宾休息室候机。 语料 Politics is usually the executive expression of human immaturity. 政治通常是人类不成熟的表现行为。（英国女作家维拉•布里顿）
[03:25.73]supervise 熟义 v. 监督；管理；指导 示例 ① Are modern parents needlessly overprotective, or is the world a more complicated and dangerous place than it was when previous generations were allowed to wander about unsupervised? 现代父母是否毫无必要地过度保护自己的孩子了呢？还是现在的世界比以前那个能够让孩子在没有大人的陪同下四处乱逛的世界更复杂、更危险了呢？（2009. 6）② He supervised the children playing near the swimming pool. 他照料着在游泳池附近玩的几个孩子。
[03:34.88]moral 熟义 a. 道德的；道义上的；品行端正的‖n. 品行；寓意 示例 ① According to Geoffrey Miller, science will offer a more practical, universal and rewarding moral framework in place of religion. 据杰弗里•米勒所说，科学将提供一个更实际的、普遍的和有益的道德构架来取代宗教。（2008. 6） ② Governments have at least a moral obligation to answer why more and more officials have a decline in moral standards. 政府至少在道义上有责任，对越来越多的官员道德水准下降这一问题做出回答。
[03:44.14]barren 熟义 a. 贫瘠的；不结果实的；不孕不育的 示例 ① Villagers tend to claim that financial compensation, where there is any, is a pittance. When land is offered as compensation it is isolated, barren and often lacks access to water, electricity, sealed roads and the like. 村民们倾向于认为财政补偿虽然在一些地方存在，但是金额少。当土地被提供作为补偿的时候，它们通常存在诸如孤立、贫瘠、用水用电困难、道路封闭等情况。（The Economist）② You can often see a barren landscape in the northwestern area of China. 在中国的西北地区，你经常会看到荒芜的景象。
[03:54.94]systematic 熟义 a. 成体系的，有条理的，有计划的，有步骤的 示例 ① If the United States wants to keep up in the global economic race, it will have to pay systematic attention to graduating minorities, not just enrolling them. 如果美国希望在全球经济中保持竞争力，它就必须系统地关注少数民族学生毕业问题，而不仅仅是录取他们。（2011. 6）② The police made a systematic search of the house. 警察对房子进行了彻底的搜查。
[04:02.92]assume 熟义 v. 假定，假设；装出，假装 示例 ① I assumed this was the way the professional world worked—cordially. 我猜想在职业世界里人们就是这样真诚友善地相处的。（2007. 12）② I had assumed her to be an English. 我本以为她是英国人。
[04:07.31]humanity 熟义 n. （统称）人类；人性；人道；博爱， 仁慈‖ [pl.]（the）humanities 人文学科 示例 ① George Herbert Mead said that humans are talked into humanity. He meant that we gain personal identity as we communicate with others. 乔治•赫伯特 •梅德说人类因交谈而具有了人性。他的意思是说，我们在与其他人交流的时候获得了个人身份。（2010. 6）② She was praised for her courage and humanity. 她的勇气和博爱受到了称赞。
[04:15.26]cyberspace 熟义 n. 网络空间 示例 ① A group of international lawyers has now published a book on the subject, under the auspices of NATO's cyber-defence centre in Tallinn. They argue that existing laws broadly apply to cyberspace. 在北大西洋公约组织驻塔林的网络防御中心的资助下，一些国际律师最近出版了一本关于这个主题的书。他们认为现有的法律同样适用于网络空间。（The Economist）② It is reported that a new electronic link-up connecting 500 hospitals around the world has checked into cyberspace. 据报道，可接通世界500 家医院的一种新型电子连接已在网络空间注册。
[04:26.55]community 熟义 n. 社区；团体；共享 示例 ① At that time we lived in a fire zone. One night a firestorm raged through and destroyed over six hundred homes in our community. 那时我们住在防火区。一天晚上一场风暴性大火肆虐，烧毁了我们社区六百多户人家的房屋。（2006. 12）② He is popular in the local community because of his unselfishness. 由于无私，他在当地社区很受欢迎。
[04:33.73]molecule 熟义 n. 分子 示例 ① A reagent of known concentration is dripped into the unknown solution in the presence of an appropriate indicator molecule. 在某种特定的指示分子的参与下，将一种已知浓度的试剂滴到未知溶液中。（The Economist）② A molecule usually consists of a group of atoms. 分子通常由一组原子构成。
[04:40.06]resort 熟义 n. 旅游胜地‖vi. 诉诸，求助 示例 ① Around the same time, I noticed that those who part with $2,285 a night to stay in a cliff-top room at the Post Ranch Inn in Big Sur, California, pay partly for the privilege of not having a TV in their rooms; the future of travel, I'm reliably told, lies in "black-hole resorts," which charge high prices precisely because you can't get online in their rooms. 与此同时， 我注意到，那些每晚舍得花费2285美元住进美国加州大苏尔海岸波斯特农庄酒店位于悬崖顶端的房间的人支付这笔费用的部分原因是为了享受他们房中没有电视的特权。我可以有把握地讲，未来的旅游在于“黑洞胜地”，那里严格地实行高价政策，因为在这些旅店的房间里你无法上网。（2012. 12）② They felt obliged to resort to laws to support their benefits. 他们觉得有必要诉诸法律来维护他们的利益。
[04:55.34]input 熟义 n. 投入资源（指时间、知识、思想等）；输入（数据、信息等） 示例 ① The amygdala receives input from many parts of the brain, including regions responsible for retrieving memories. 扁桃腺从大脑的很多部分——包括负责恢复记忆的区域——接收信息。（2006. 12）② I think language learning requires a great mount of input and output. 我认为学习语言需要大量的输入和输出。
[05:02.55]critic 熟义 n. 批评家，评论员；挑剔的人 示例 ① Democrats and Republicans can and will take sides on a number of issues, but a more crucial concern is that both are basing major policy decisions on guesstimates rather than looking at the vast wealth of raw data with a critical eye and an open mind. 民主党人和共和党人可以并且愿意偏袒许多问题，但更关键的问题在于，双方都基于猜测性的估计来做出重大的政策决定，而不是用批判性的眼光和开放的心态来研究大量的原始数据。（2013. 6） ② In this article, the drama critic commented upon all the plays he had seen. 这位戏剧评论员在这篇文章中点评了他看过的所有戏剧。
[05:14.18]astonish 熟义 v. 使十分惊讶，使吃惊 示例 ① If viewers cast aside their hostility, what may astonish is Mr. Hirst's ability to transform dry conceptual art into witty, emotionally engaging work. 观众如果抛开敌意，可能会震惊于赫斯特把枯燥的概念艺术转变成诙谐而富有情感魅力的作品的能力。（The Economist）② The news that they got divorced astonished everyone. 他俩离婚的消息使大家十分惊讶。
[05:21.93]flip 熟义 v.（使）快速翻转；按（开关、按钮等）；（用手指）轻弹 示例 ① There are some bright spots for them, such as North Carolina, where the newly Republican legislature is likely to be able to flip a few Democratic seats in Congress by rejigging the boundaries. 有些地方他们有明显优势，比如北卡罗来纳州，新的共和党立法机构可能通过改变选区界限，争取一些现属民主党的席位。（The Economist）② He flipped to the index and found the information he needed. 他翻到索引，找到了所需的资料。
[05:31.36]definite 熟义 a. 确定的；清楚的；有把握的 示例 ① A study by Mannaz, a leadership development company, suggests that, while the bully-boy chief executive of old may not have been eradicated completely, there is a definite shift in emphasis towards less tough styles of management —at least in America and Europe. 一项由处于领军地位的马南兹发展公司所开展的调查研究显示，虽然过去那种粗暴的主管可能不会彻底消失，但是确实已有所改变，开始强调采用不那么强硬的管理模式——至少在美国和欧洲是如此。（2011. 6）② We have very definite ideas on how to bring up excellent students. 关于如何培养优秀的学生我们有非常明确的想法。
